# AI Search Portal Standards

**Tool adapter**: Project truth and agent capabilities live in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and [AGENT_CAPABILITIES.md](../../AGENT_CAPABILITIES.md). This file extends those canonical sources; it must not override them. Keep in sync with AGENTS.md.

This portal is the **skeleton for aggregating and organizing information systems**. Feature and route design should stay modular and thin. See `collaboration-architecture.mdc` for directory, data flow, and CI alignment. Conventions: `docs/conventions/`, `docs/README.md`.

## Workflow
- Run `pnpm run lint`, `pnpm run typecheck`, `pnpm run test` before PR.
- Use `pnpm run changeset` for user-facing changes.

## Architecture
- **Two pillars**：Clean architecture with docs/product as spec hub (`docs/architecture/clean-architecture.md`); semi-automated UI via design system (`docs/architecture/design-system.md`, `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`).
- **Five layers**（`docs/architecture/repo-layers.md`）：**app** (shell: routes, root, entry) → **features** → **components** (ui/shared/app) → **services** (`app/services/*`, `app/shared/*`) → **infra** (optional). Features must not depend on other features; components must not depend on features.
- **Design system / Figma MCP**（`docs/architecture/figma-mcp.md`）：Token canonical 在 repo。使用 Figma MCP 時：僅可更新既有 token 數值與 docs，不可新增 primitive token（未定義 token 標記待人工確認）；不新增 UI component 或 primitive variant，新增須人工確認；不依 Figma frame 生成或修改 layout，layout 權威在 repo。見 AGENT_CAPABILITIES.md 與 figma-mcp §4。
- Feature code in `app/features/*` (hooks/server/types).
- Shared code in `app/shared/*`, app services in `app/services/*`.
- Routes in `app/routes/*` only coordinate UI + data flow.

## File and folder naming (mandatory)
- **Folders** under `app/` (except under `app/routes`): **lowercase only**, no hyphen/underscore (e.g. `chat`, `ui`, `errorboundary`). Do **not** use `error-boundary` or `errorBoundary`.
- **Component files** under `app/components/**/*.tsx`: **PascalCase** filename (e.g. `ErrorBoundaryFallback.tsx`, `ChatInterface.tsx`). Barrel files: `index.ts` is allowed.
- Naming is enforced by `pnpm run lint:filenames` in CI and pre-commit. When creating or renaming files/folders, follow these rules so the check passes. See `docs/CONVENTIONS.md` and `docs/conventions/coding-conventions.md` for full rules.

## Coding Standards
- Avoid `any` and unsafe casts; fix or narrow types.
- Keep imports sorted (ESLint handles this).
- Use `??` when values can be nullish.
- Remove unused imports/vars.

## Testing
- Vitest + Testing Library for unit/UI tests.
- MSW handlers in `app/test/handlers.ts`; keep network isolated.

## Dependencies
- Baseline: React 18. When adding or upgrading packages, check peer/react support and update `docs/conventions/packages-react.md`. Run `npm ls react react-dom` to catch peer conflicts before PR.

## Commits
- Conventional Commits required (commitlint enforces). When deleting tracked files, use `git rm <path>` to preserve history; see `docs/conventions/git-version-control.md`.
